&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Browserbase&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Browserbase is the complete platform for building and deploying AI agents that browse and interact with the web like humans. With a single API key, developers can enable agents to search and retrieve information, fill out forms, and take action across websites. Today, Browserbase powers more than 50 million browser sessions each month for over 10,000 customers, including Ramp, DeepMind, Clay, Vercel, and Notion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a Series B startup that&#39;s tripled our headcount in 2 years, and we&#39;re continuing to grow, fast. Backed by Kleiner Perkins, CRV, and Notable Capital, our team is building on our CEO&#39;s&lt;a href=&quot;https://memos.hawkhill.ventures/p/an-internet-browser-for-ai&quot;&gt; founding vision&lt;/a&gt; to power the world&#39;s best AI tools and help everyone automate the web.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be one of the first Mid Market Account Executives at Browserbase, and you&#39;ll help build this segment from the ground up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mid Market is where some of the most exciting AI work is happening right now. Companies with 100 to 2,999 employees are moving fast, putting agents into production, and making real infrastructure bets. They need a partner who understands the technology and can guide them from first build to company-wide rollout. That partner is you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll run full-cycle deals with multiple stakeholders, from the engineers building with Browserbase to the leaders signing the contract. You&#39;ll land new logos, set them up to expand, and help turn promising accounts into some of our largest customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll also work directly with GTM leadership to define how we win in Mid Market: who we target, how we qualify, how we price and package, and how we land and expand. The playbook you write will shape every Mid Market hire that follows.&amp;nbsp;If you want real ownership, bigger deals and a hand in building a segment, this is the seat.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Mid Market segment: run full-cycle deals with companies of 100 to 2,999 employees, from prospecting to signed contract.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Land and expand: win new logos, then build the relationships and roadmap that turn first deals into larger, multi-team commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build pipeline: combine inbound, product-led signals and strategic outbound to create a healthy, growing pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Convert product-led growth: identify self-serve teams with momentum and turn them into strategic, committed contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multithread every deal: build trust with engineers, engineering leaders, security, procurement and executive buyers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the playbook: create the processes, messaging and qualification standards that define how Mid Market sells at Browserbase.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run compelling, technical demos: partner with Solutions Engineering to show how Browserbase solves real business problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate and close: lead pricing, contract and security conversations through the full sales cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the product: bring customer feedback, use cases and competitive intel back to Product and Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Forecast with precision: track your metrics, report on pipeline and call your number accurately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the face of Browserbase: represent us at events, conferences and customer meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You Might Be a Good Fit If You Have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of closing experience in SaaS, ideally selling technical or AI infrastructure products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of exceeding quota selling into mid-size companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running multi-stakeholder deals, including security reviews and procurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with product-led growth, specifically converting self-serve users into contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with outbound prospecting and building your own pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical aptitude and the ability to talk credibly with developers and engineering leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, written and verbal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivation and comfort operating in ambiguity at a fast-growing startup.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to work from our San Francisco HQ 4 days a week (or willingness to relocate).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling dev tools, APIs or infrastructure to technical buyers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building sales processes or a new segment from scratch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A history of land-and-expand wins that grew into large accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why Join Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build something that matters.&lt;/strong&gt; Work on a product developers love (just look at @browserbase).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape a segment from day one.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll help define the Mid Market motion, the role and the playbook that future reps inherit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grow with the company.&lt;/strong&gt; Early GTM hires here have a real path to lead, mentor and build the team as we scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lean, high-impact team.&lt;/strong&gt; Your deals move the company forward, and everyone sees it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Benefits&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and early-stage equity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive medical, dental and vision coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Catered lunches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Downtown San Francisco office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI tools and credits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team offsites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;OTE (includes base + commission)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$219,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$274,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Browserbase is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you need a reasonable accommodation at any point during the application or interview process, please contact your recruiter.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Browserbase&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Browserbase is the complete platform for building and deploying AI agents that browse and interact with the web like humans. With a single API key, developers can enable agents to search and retrieve information, fill out forms, and take action across websites. Today, Browserbase powers more than 50 million browser sessions each month for over 10,000 customers, including Ramp, DeepMind, Clay, Vercel, and Notion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a Series B startup that&#39;s tripled our headcount in 2 years, and we&#39;re continuing to grow, fast. Backed by Kleiner Perkins, CRV, and Notable Capital, our team is building on our CEO&#39;s&lt;a href=&quot;https://memos.hawkhill.ventures/p/an-internet-browser-for-ai&quot;&gt; founding vision&lt;/a&gt; to power the world&#39;s best AI tools and help everyone automate the web.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be one of the first Velocity Account Executives at Browserbase, and you&#39;ll help define what this role and this segment become.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Velocity motion is where the action is fastest. Developers sign up, start building, and hit real scale on their own. Your job is to find those teams at exactly the right moment and turn momentum into committed contracts. That means a high volume of deals, shorter sales cycles, and the chance to close more new logos in a quarter than most AEs close in a year.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work directly with GTM leadership to build the playbook from the ground up: how we spot product-led signals, how we qualify fast, how we price and package for speed, and how we hand off to expansion. What you build here becomes the foundation every future Velocity rep runs on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you love speed, reps and a fast scoreboard, this is the seat.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a high-velocity book: run a large volume of opportunities from first touch to signed contract, with short cycles and fast decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Convert product-led momentum: use usage data and signals to identify self-serve teams ready to scale, then turn them into annual and committed-use contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prospect relentlessly: pair inbound and product signals with sharp outbound to keep your pipeline full every week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the playbook: create the processes, talk tracks, sequences and qualification standards that define how Velocity sells at Browserbase.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run tight, technical demos: partner with Solutions Engineering when needed, and show developers exactly how Browserbase fits into what they&#39;re building.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Close with speed: negotiate pricing and terms efficiently and manage the full cycle without letting deals stall.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the product: bring customer feedback, use cases and competitive intel back to Product and Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Forecast with precision: track your metrics, report on pipeline and call your number accurately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the face of Browserbase: represent us at events, hackathons and in developer communities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You Might Be a Good Fit If You Have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of closing experience in SaaS, ideally selling technical or AI infrastructure products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of exceeding quota in a high-volume, short-cycle motion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with product-led growth, specifically converting self-serve users into paying contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort and energy for outbound prospecting and running many deals at once.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical aptitude and the ability to talk credibly with developers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, written and verbal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivation and comfort operating in ambiguity at a fast-growing startup.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to work from our San Francisco HQ 4 days a week (or willingness to relocate).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling dev tools, APIs or infrastructure to technical buyers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience helping build a sales process or segment from scratch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A love for metrics, experiments and finding the fastest path to yes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why Join Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build something that matters. Work on a product developers love (just look at @browserbase).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape a segment from day one. You&#39;ll help define the Velocity motion, the role and the playbook that future reps inherit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow with the company. Early GTM hires here have a real path to lead, mentor and build the team as we scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lean, high-impact team. Your wins show up on the board every week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Benefits&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and early-stage equity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive medical, dental and vision coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Catered lunches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Downtown San Francisco office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI tools and credits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team offsites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;OTE (includes base + commission)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$178,500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$223,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Browserbase is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you need a reasonable accommodation at any point during the application or interview process, please contact your recruiter.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Browserbase&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Browserbase is the complete platform for building and deploying AI agents that browse and interact with the web like humans. With a single API key, developers can enable agents to search and retrieve information, fill out forms, and take action across websites. Today, Browserbase powers more than 50 million browser sessions each month for over 10,000 customers, including Ramp, DeepMind, Clay, Vercel, and Notion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a Series B startup that&#39;s tripled our headcount in 2 years, and we&#39;re continuing to grow, fast. Backed by Kleiner Perkins, CRV, and Notable Capital, our team is building on our CEO&#39;s&lt;a href=&quot;https://memos.hawkhill.ventures/p/an-internet-browser-for-ai&quot;&gt; founding vision&lt;/a&gt; to power the world&#39;s best AI tools and help everyone automate the web.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Job Title: Chief of Staff&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Worksite Location: 1 Post S, Floor 15, San Francisco, CA 94104&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Job Description&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as CEO’s key strategic partner in defining company direction, partnering directly with C-suite leadership to align commercial strategy with business objectives and drive market entry, aligning cross-functional initiatives, and executing high-impact business decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive competitive intelligence and market analysis to inform product positioning and capture market share in developer infrastructure, conducting in-depth competitive analysis of the industry landscape using SQL and Python-based modeling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define strategic buyer personas and messaging frameworks for developers, CTOs, and enterprise tech leaders (Python/SQL, AI).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architecting and executing scalable go-to-market strategy tailored to headless browser, dev-centric infrastructure markets, and full-funnel marketing campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish performance metrics and KPIs that drive strategic marketing decision-making and growth accountability, developing dynamic revenue forecasting models and commission calculation frameworks to support financial planning, quota-setting, and performance accountability using Stripe Sigma, SQL, and Python.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate high-impact partnership agreements that accelerate growth and market penetration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive co-marketing initiatives and joint value propositions with key ecosystem players.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement scalable marketing systems (CRM, project management) that support rapid growth using Hubspot, Apollo.io, Sales Navigator and Hunter.io.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional collaboration between engineering, product, and go-to-market teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;May telecommute&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Minimum Requirements:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master’s (or foreign educ. equiv.) Degree in Computer, Information, and Technology,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Management Information Systems, Information Technology, Business Administration, or a&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;related field plus two (2) years’ experience in the job offered or related occupation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Special Skill Requirements:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architecting and executing go-to-market strategy and full-funnel marketing campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnering directly with C-suite leadership to align commercial strategy with business objectives and drive market entry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conducting in-depth competitive analysis of the industry landscape using SQL and Python-based modeling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Using Stripe Sigma, SQL, and Python.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing dynamic revenue forecasting models and commission calculation frameworks to support financial planning, quota-setting, and performance accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Using Hubspot, Apollo.io, Sales Navigator and Hunter.io.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base Salary: $225,000 per annum. 40 hours per week; M-F.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Browserbase is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you need a reasonable accommodation at any point during the application or interview process, please contact your recruiter.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Browserbase&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Browserbase is the complete platform for building and deploying AI agents that browse and interact with the web like humans. With a single API key, developers can enable agents to search and retrieve information, fill out forms, and take action across websites. Today, Browserbase powers more than 50 million browser sessions each month for over 10,000 customers, including Ramp, DeepMind, Clay, Vercel, and Notion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a Series B startup that&#39;s tripled our headcount in 2 years, and we&#39;re continuing to grow, fast. Backed by Kleiner Perkins, CRV, and Notable Capital, our team is building on our CEO&#39;s&lt;a href=&quot;https://memos.hawkhill.ventures/p/an-internet-browser-for-ai&quot;&gt; founding vision&lt;/a&gt; to power the world&#39;s best AI tools and help everyone automate the web.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 data-pm-slice=&quot;0 0 []&quot;&gt;About &lt;strong&gt;Browserbase&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Browserbase is the complete platform to build and deploy agents that browse and interact with the web like humans. We’re on a mission to make AI work for people by operating the systems built for humans. We provide one API key for agents to search and fetch information, fill out forms, and replicate user actions. We run 50M+ sessions/month for 10,000+ customers including Ramp, Deepmind, Clay, Vercel, and Notion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a Series B startup that&#39;s tripled our headcount in 2 years, and are continuing to grow, fast. Backed by Kleiner Perkins, CRV, and Notable Capital, our team is building on our CEO&#39;s&lt;a href=&quot;https://memos.hawkhill.ventures/p/an-internet-browser-for-ai&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt; &lt;u&gt;founding vision&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; to power the world&#39;s best AI tools and help everyone automate the web.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Content Lead to own our content-led-growth engine. This role would oversee all awareness activities across blogs, docs, socials, SEO, and launches to fuel our top of funnel. You&#39;ll craft the point of view that makes developers and technical buyers understand our category and product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re a great fit for this role if you’ve been in Product Marketing, Content Strategy, Growth Engineering, or Brand Marketing. You love telling stories, writing, and have great taste. And of course, you’ve been an engineer or can market to one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive the content strategy&lt;/strong&gt; and bar for Browserbase across organic &amp;amp; paid channels to hit our growth goals and measure success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define the market&lt;/strong&gt; we’re operating in and the thought leadership we need to own it, in partnership with our Product Marketers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run and grow a team&lt;/strong&gt; that spans content, product marketing, and developer experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Review and create content&lt;/strong&gt; that developers actually want to read and share.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work on strategic technical partnerships&lt;/strong&gt; for where Browserbase can integrate with other tools. This includes integrations, documentation, and co-marketing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner with Sales, Product, and Growth&lt;/strong&gt; making sure content performs, converts, and is useful across the funnel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Represent Browserbase&lt;/strong&gt; in high-visibility moments like launches, executive writing, PR, and Partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;7+ years in content or brand marketing at a developer-facing company, with execution and strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A track record of building content programs that moved pipeline and revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fluency across Twitter, LinkedIn, Reddit, and Hacker News.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong SEO instincts and comfort with paid content and distribution, not just organic.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Excellent writing and editing, with a clear point of view on what makes writing good.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience managing and growing a team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A real interest in the browser automation and AI agent space, and the judgment to translate that into a market narrative.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ve led content at a company through a major market shift or category creation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ve written or ghostwritten for executives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Competitive salary + meaningful early-stage equity&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage for you and your dependents&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;401(k)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Daily catered lunches with a fully-stocked kitchen&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beautiful office in downtown San Francisco&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All the AI tools + credits you want&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Regular team offsites and company events&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Base Compensation&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$215,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$260,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Browserbase is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
