&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Browserbase&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Browserbase is the complete platform for building and deploying AI agents that browse and interact with the web like humans. With a single API key, developers can enable agents to search and retrieve information, fill out forms, and take action across websites. Today, Browserbase powers more than 50 million browser sessions each month for over 10,000 customers, including Ramp, DeepMind, Clay, Vercel, and Notion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a Series B startup that&#39;s tripled our headcount in 2 years, and we&#39;re continuing to grow, fast. Backed by Kleiner Perkins, CRV, and Notable Capital, our team is building on our CEO&#39;s&lt;a href=&quot;https://memos.hawkhill.ventures/p/an-internet-browser-for-ai&quot;&gt; founding vision&lt;/a&gt; to power the world&#39;s best AI tools and help everyone automate the web.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Technical Recruiter to help build our Engineering, Product and Design teams at Browserbase. You’ll own full cycle technical recruiting from initial intake through offer acceptance, partnering closely with hiring managers to understand what their teams need and find people who can make a meaningful impact as we grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll bring curiosity, strong judgment, intentionality, and a high level of ownership to every search. You care about understanding the work behind a job description, building relationships with talented people, and helping teams make thoughtful hiring decisions. You take pride in both the people you hire and the experience you create for every candidate, regardless of the outcome.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own technical hiring from start to finish.&lt;/strong&gt; Lead the full recruiting process across engineering and other technical functions, including intake, sourcing, screening, and closing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build strong hiring manager partnerships.&lt;/strong&gt; Align on role expectations, candidate profiles, and interview plans. Bring recommendations, ask thoughtful questions, and help hiring managers make clear, timely decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Source with intention.&lt;/strong&gt; Build targeted sourcing strategies that reflect each team’s needs and the company’s long-term goals. Develop relationships with candidates whose experience, interests, and ways of working align with the opportunity.&lt;/li&gt;
